  "root_cause": {
    "text": "The `nf_flow_table_offload` subsystem failed to validate action counts against the maximum limit in `flow_action_entry_next()`, permitting valid IPv6 offload configurations requiring more than 16 actions to write beyond the allocated action entries array.",
    "evidence": "The patch increases `NF_FLOW_RULE_ACTION_MAX` from 16 to 24, adds a bounds check in `flow_action_entry_next()` returning NULL upon reaching the limit, and propagates `-E2BIG` errors to callers to prevent out-of-bounds writes.",
    "passed_review": false
  },
  "vuln_statements": [],
  "agent_logs": [
    {
      "root_cause_candidate": "The netfilter flow table offload code lacked bounds checking in `flow_action_entry_next()`, allowing the number of hardware offload actions to exceed the allocated array size (originally 16) for complex IPv6 flows, resulting in out-of-bounds memory writes.",
      "evidence_points": "The patch introduces a check `if (unlikely(flow_rule->rule->action.num_entries >= NF_FLOW_RULE_ACTION_MAX)) return NULL;` in `flow_action_entry_next()`, increases the limit from 16 to 24, and ensures callers handle the NULL return by aborting the offload setup with `-E2BIG` errors."
    },
    {
